What the planner should know first:

1. The yoagent 0.27.3 → 0.27.4 upgrade has been rolled back every session since 19:50 (#1152). One test, temperature_support::tests::built_config_sampling_flag_table, still expects the 0.27.3 behaviour. The issue calls the fix "test only", but that's incomplete. Once on 0.27.4, temperature is also dropped for GPT-6 ids (per yoagent's changelog). Our note in src/temperature_support.rs is hardcoded to say "Anthropic removed temperature for Claude 4.7 and later". So a GPT-6 user who sets --temperature would see a note blaming Anthropic for an OpenAI model. The upgrade task should fix that wording too. That test also stops at its first failing row, so every row after it needs re-running.
2. #1127 is down to 3 shell verbs, and I confirmed them on the built binary. yoyo lint --bogus, yoyo skill bogus and yoyo map --bogus still tell shell users to type slash commands. The fix pattern already exists from the earlier verbs.
3. Two files are close to the size limit, and going over reverts the whole task. src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines away (and not on the exceptions list); src/help.rs is 10 lines away. The three #1127 files have 49–80 lines of room.
4. #1147 is the next slice of the made-up model ids. About 24 offered ids are unchecked. They should be checked against an outside source as a whole set, not a hand-picked shortlist.
5. Two decisions are waiting on @yuanhao, so neither should be planned: #1094 item 1 (overwriting a file that was never read) and #1149 (-p approving every tool call).

